      "content": "I strongly advise against giving your child additional salt to make the juice sweeter or more palatable, as excessive salt can exacerbate dehydration and even lead to serious complications. The recommended amounts of salt for homemade Pedialyte are: 1/4 teaspoon of salt in 1 cup of water, or adding 1/4 teaspoon of sugar per 1 ounce of juice. However, I still strongly encourage you to consult a medical professional or a pediatrician for personalized advice, as their online or phone advice is more likely to be specific to your child's situation.",
